// Emergency utterances (10 cases). HARD GATE — zero routings, no exceptions.
//
// Stage 6 of the pipeline is non-negotiable: a teacher describing an active
// emergency reaches the existing emergency coach prompt with zero added latency
// and zero chance of being routed into a worksheet form. M5 proved it by
// latency (87 ms against ~1.2 s for a routed utterance) as well as by asserting
// zero recorded Gemini calls.
//
// ─── A FINDING THIS STRATUM IS DELIBERATELY SHAPED TO SURFACE ───────────────
// `EMERGENCY_SITUATION_PATTERNS` in safety/inputGuard.js is ENGLISH-ONLY. A
// teacher describing the same emergency in Hindi or Hinglish does NOT trip the
// short-circuit, so the classifier does run and the response arrives by the
// ordinary passthrough path instead.
//
// The last three cases are labelled to that reality rather than to the reality
// anyone would prefer, and they are labelled WITHOUT `passthroughReason` so the
// integrity test can assert the split in both directions: every case claiming
// `emergency_detected` must trip the guard, and every case not claiming it must
// not. The router-safety property still holds for all ten — nothing is routed
// into a form — but the zero-latency guarantee holds only for the English seven.
//
// inputGuard.js is a PROTECTED file (area 11): consumed, never adjusted. This is
// recorded as a finding for the owner, not fixed here.

